IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-possession.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Possession and Trafficking": sections 354 to 360.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 355.1 ...`, `s 787(1) ...`); never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Possession and Trafficking (ss 354 to 360)`

§§ `Section 354 -- possession of property obtained by crime`

-- src:6930 | Possession of property obtained by crime
-- src:6931 | 354 (1) Every one commits an offence who has in his possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property or thing or of the proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from
-- src:6932 | (a) the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment; or
-- src:6933 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 354(1) (src:6930-6933)
GIVEN `the person has in their possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 354(1) the person commits the offence of possession of property obtained by crime` MEANS
    IF    `the person has in their possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing`
      AND (   `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment`
           OR `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who has in his possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property or thing or of the proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from"

-- src:6934 | Obliterated vehicle identification number
-- src:6935 | (2) In proceedings in respect of an offence under subsection (1), evidence that a person has in their possession a motor vehicle the vehicle identification number of which has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated or a part of a motor vehicle being a part bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the motor vehicle or part, as the case may be, was obtained,
-- src:6936 | (a) by the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment; or
-- src:6937 | (b) by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 354(2) (src:6934-6937)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 354(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the person has in their possession a motor vehicle the vehicle identification number of which has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 354(2) the evidence is proof that the motor vehicle or part was obtained by an offence punishable by indictment` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are in respect of an offence under subsection 354(1)`
      AND `there is evidence that the person has in their possession a motor vehicle the vehicle identification number of which has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated, or a part of a motor vehicle bearing a vehicle identification number that has been wholly or partially removed or obliterated`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that the motor vehicle or part, as the case may be, was obtained"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of evidence of possession of a motor vehicle or part whose vehicle identification number has been removed or obliterated, in proceedings in respect of an offence under (1)

-- src:6938 | Definition of vehicle identification number
-- src:6939 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), vehicle identification number means any number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle for the purpose of distinguishing the motor vehicle from other similar motor vehicles.
@ref Criminal Code s 354(3) (src:6938-6939)
GIVEN `it is a number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is placed for the purpose of distinguishing the motor vehicle from other similar motor vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 354(3) the number or mark is a vehicle identification number` MEANS
    IF `it is a number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle` AND `it is placed for the purpose of distinguishing the motor vehicle from other similar motor vehicles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "vehicle identification number means any number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle for the purpose of distinguishing the motor vehicle from other similar motor vehicles"

-- src:6940 | Exception
-- src:6941 | (4) A peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer is not guilty of an offence under this section by reason only that the peace officer or person possesses property or a thing or the proceeds of property or a thing mentioned in subsection (1) for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer’s duties.
@ref Criminal Code s 354(4) (src:6940-6941)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person acting under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses the property or thing or the proceeds of the property or thing for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 354(4) the person is guilty of an offence under section 354 by reason only of possessing the property for the purposes of an investigation or in the execution of the peace officer's duties` MEANS
    IF `the person possesses the property or thing or the proceeds of the property or thing for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer's duties`
    THEN CONSIDER `ccc12 or` `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` (JUST `the person is a person acting under the direction of a peace officer`)
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A peace officer or a person acting under the direction of a peace officer is not guilty of an offence under this section by reason only that the peace officer or person possesses property or a thing or the proceeds of property or a thing mentioned in subsection (1) for the purposes of an investigation or otherwise in the execution of the peace officer’s duties"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for a peace officer or a person acting under a peace officer's direction
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "peace officer" answer was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that" the possession is for the purposes of an investigation or in the execution of the officer's duties

§§ `Sections 355 to 355.5 -- punishment, traffic, trafficking, in rem prohibition`

-- 355: "(a) if the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or the value of the subject matter of the offence is more than $5,000 ... (b) if the value ... is not more than $5,000 ..."
-- src:6942 | Punishment
-- src:6943 | 355 Every one who commits an offence under section 354
-- src:6944 | (a) if the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument or the value of the subject matter of the offence is more than $5,000, is guilty of
-- src:6945 | (i) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, or
-- src:6946 | (ii) an offence punishable on summary conviction; or
-- src:6947 | (b) if the value of the subject matter of the offence is not more than $5,000, is guilty
-- src:6948 | (i) of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or
-- src:6949 | (ii) of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 355 (src:6942-6949)
GIVEN `the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 355 the punishment for the offence under section 354` MEANS
    CONSIDER `ccc12 or` `the subject matter of the offence is a testamentary instrument, by s 2 testamentary instrument` (JUST (`the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
                                  , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (a)(ii)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (b)(i) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years
                                   , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- (b)(ii)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "testamentary instrument" answer was not given and the value is not more than $5,000

-- src:6950 | Definition of traffic
-- src:6951 | 355.1 For the purposes of sections 355.2 and 355.4, traffic means to sell, give, transfer, transport, export from Canada, import into Canada, send, deliver or deal with in any other way, or to offer to do any of those acts.
@ref Criminal Code s 355.1 (src:6950-6951)
GIVEN `the person sells, gives, transfers, transports, exports from Canada, imports into Canada, sends, delivers or deals with in any other way the property or thing, or offers to do any of those acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355.1 the person traffics` MEANS
    IF `the person sells, gives, transfers, transports, exports from Canada, imports into Canada, sends, delivers or deals with in any other way the property or thing, or offers to do any of those acts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "traffic means to sell, give, transfer, transport, export from Canada, import into Canada, send, deliver or deal with in any other way, or to offer to do any of those acts"

-- src:6952 | Trafficking in property obtained by crime
-- src:6953 | 355.2 Everyone commits an offence who traffics in any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from
-- src:6954 | (a) the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment; or
-- src:6955 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 355.2 (src:6952-6955)
GIVEN `the person traffics in any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing, by s 355.1 the person traffics` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355.2 the person commits the offence of trafficking in property obtained by crime` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the person traffics in any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing, by s 355.1 the person traffics`
                (JUST (    `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment`
                        OR `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`))
    -- JUST FALSE where the person does not traffic or does not know: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who traffics in any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 355.1 answer was not given

-- src:6956 | In rem prohibition
-- src:6957 | 355.3 The importation into Canada or exportation from Canada of any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing is prohibited if all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from
-- src:6958 | (a) the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment; or
-- src:6959 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 355.3 (src:6956-6959)
GIVEN `the act is the importation into Canada or exportation from Canada of any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355.3 the importation or exportation is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act is the importation into Canada or exportation from Canada of any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section prohibits "the importation into Canada or exportation from Canada"; another act is outside it
        IF    `all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment`
           OR `all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is prohibited if all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from" (a bar whose gate is unmet)

-- src:6960 | Possession of property obtained by crime — trafficking
-- src:6961 | 355.4 Everyone commits an offence who has in their possession, for the purpose of trafficking, any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from
-- src:6962 | (a) the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment; or
-- src:6963 | (b) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment.
@ref Criminal Code s 355.4 (src:6960-6963)
GIVEN `the person has in their possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the possession is for the purpose of trafficking, by s 355.1 the person traffics` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 355.4 the person commits the offence of possession of property obtained by crime for the purpose of trafficking` MEANS
    IF    `the person has in their possession any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing`
      AND (   `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission in Canada of an offence punishable by indictment`
           OR `the person knows that all or part of it was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence punishable by indictment`)
    THEN `the possession is for the purpose of trafficking, by s 355.1 the person traffics`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 355.1 answer was not given; JUST FALSE where it is a definite no
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who has in their possession, for the purpose of trafficking, any property or thing or any proceeds of any property or thing knowing that all or part of the property, thing or proceeds was obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from"

-- 355.5: (a) value more than $5,000: indictable, not more than 14 years (no summary limb); (b) value not more than $5,000: indictable, not more than five years, or summary.
-- src:6964 | Punishment
-- src:6965 | 355.5 Everyone who commits an offence under section 355.2 or 355.4
-- src:6966 | (a) is, if the value of the subject matter of the offence is more than $5,000, guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years; or
-- src:6967 | (b) is, if the value of the subject matter of the offence is not more than $5,000,
-- src:6968 | (i) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years, or
-- src:6969 | (ii) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 355.5 (src:6964-6969)
GIVEN `the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 355.5 the punishment for the offence under section 355.2 or 355.4` MEANS
    IF `the value of the subject matter of the offence, in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000
    THEN LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)   -- (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years
    ELSE LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)   -- (b)(i) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years
              , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b)(ii) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction

§§ `Sections 356 to 360 -- theft from mail, bringing in, having in possession`

-- src:6970 | Theft from mail
-- src:6971 | 356 (1) Everyone commits an offence who
-- src:6972 | (a) steals
-- src:6973 | (i) anything sent by post, after it is deposited at a post office and before it is delivered, or after it is delivered but before it is in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail,
-- src:6974 | (ii) a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail, or
-- src:6975 | (iii) a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation;
-- src:6976 | (a.1) with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a), makes, possesses or uses a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail;
-- src:6977 | (b) has in their possession anything that they know has been used to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (a.1) or anything in respect of which they know that such an offence has been committed; or
-- src:6978 | (c) fraudulently redirects, or causes to be redirected, anything sent by post.
@ref Criminal Code s 356(1) (src:6970-6978)
GIVEN `the person steals, by s 2 steal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is deposited at a post office and before it is delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is delivered but before it is in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a), the person makes, possesses or uses a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in their possession anything that they know has been used to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (a.1) or anything in respect of which they know that such an offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently redirects, or causes to be redirected, anything sent by post` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(1) the person commits the offence of theft from mail` MEANS
    `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `paragraph (a)` (JUST `paragraph (a.1)`)) (JUST (`paragraph (b)` OR `paragraph (c)`))
    -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who (a) steals"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "steal" answer was not given and no other paragraph holds
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `ccc12 and` `the person steals, by s 2 steal`
                        (JUST (    `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is deposited at a post office and before it is delivered`
                                OR `the thing is anything sent by post, after it is delivered but before it is in the possession of the addressee or of a person who may reasonably be considered to be authorized by the addressee to receive mail`
                                OR `the thing is a bag, sack or other container or covering in which mail is conveyed, whether or not it contains mail`
                                OR `the thing is a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation`))
        `paragraph (a.1)` MEANS `with intent to commit an offence under paragraph (a), the person makes, possesses or uses a copy of a key suited to a lock adopted for use by the Canada Post Corporation, or a key suited to obtaining access to a receptacle or device provided for the receipt of mail`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS `the person has in their possession anything that they know has been used to commit an offence under paragraph (a) or (a.1) or anything in respect of which they know that such an offence has been committed`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS `the person fraudulently redirects, or causes to be redirected, anything sent by post`

-- src:6979 | Allegation of value not necessary
-- src:6980 | (2) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is not necessary to allege in the indictment or to prove on the trial that anything in respect of which the offence was committed had any value.
@ref Criminal Code s 356(2) (src:6979-6980)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings for an offence under section 356` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 356(2) it is necessary to allege in the indictment or to prove on the trial that the thing had any value` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings for an offence under section 356`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In proceedings for an offence under this section it is not necessary to allege in the indictment or to prove on the trial that anything in respect of which the offence was committed had any value"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of proceedings for an offence under section 356

-- src:6981 | Punishment
-- src:6982 | (3) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:6983 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:6984 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 356(3) (src:6981-6984)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 356(3) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6985 | Bringing into Canada property obtained by crime
-- src:6986 | 357 Every person who brings into or has in Canada anything that they have obtained outside Canada by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354 is guilty of
-- src:6987 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:6988 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 357 (src:6985-6988)
GIVEN `the person brings into or has in Canada anything` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained it outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 357 the person commits the offence of bringing into Canada property obtained by crime` MEANS
    IF    `the person brings into or has in Canada anything`
      AND `the person obtained it outside Canada`
      AND `the person obtained it by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who brings into or has in Canada anything that they have obtained outside Canada by an act that, if it had been committed in Canada, would have been the offence of theft or an offence under section 342 or 354"

@ref Criminal Code s 357 (src:6986-6988)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 357 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- 358: "For the purposes of sections 342 and 354 and paragraph 356(1)(b), the offence of having in possession is complete when ..." An offence outside the list is NOTHING; "when" counts as "where" (fork F-WHEN).
-- src:6989 | Having in possession when complete
-- src:6990 | 358 For the purposes of sections 342 and 354 and paragraph 356(1)(b), the offence of having in possession is complete when a person has, alone or jointly with another person, possession of or control over anything mentioned in those sections or when he aids in concealing or disposing of it, as the case may be.
@ref Criminal Code s 358 (src:6989-6990)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, possession of anything mentioned in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, control over anything mentioned in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person aids in concealing or disposing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 358 the offence of having in possession is complete` MEANS
    IF `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 342 OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 354 OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 356 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(b)")
    THEN IF    `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, possession of anything mentioned in those sections`
            OR `the person has, alone or jointly with another person, control over anything mentioned in those sections`
            OR `the person aids in concealing or disposing of it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offence of having in possession is complete when a person has, alone or jointly with another person, possession of or control over anything mentioned in those sections or when he aids in concealing or disposing of it, as the case may be"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 342 and 354 and paragraph 356(1)(b)"; any other offence is outside the list

-- src:6991 | 359 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 40]
@ref Criminal Code s 359 (src:6991)
`s 359 as the text shows it` MEANS "359 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 40]"

-- src:6992 | 360 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 40]
@ref Criminal Code s 360 (src:6992)
`s 360 as the text shows it` MEANS "360 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 40]"
